# Drive a real application: open Notepad, type with synthetic keystrokes and
# save the file through Notepad's own Save dialog. After a run there should be
# a hawk-note.txt in your Documents folder containing exactly the typed line.
#
# Try it safely first:  hawk.exe --dry-run --file examples\notepad-demo.hawk
# Then for real:        hawk.exe --file examples\notepad-demo.hawk
#
# Hold ESC or press Ctrl+Alt+H at any point to abort.

open notepad
wait 2200
focus Notepad

type Hawk OS typed this with real keystrokes, then saved it.
wait 400

key ctrl+s
wait 1800
type hawk-note.txt
key enter
wait 1800

shot notepad-result.png
windows 6

log Notepad demo complete - the file should hold the typed line
